ndards.</li><li>Grown using <strong>sustainable farming methods</strong>, ensuring <strong>long-term supply stability</strong>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Cost-Effective Raw Material Source</strong><ul><li><strong>Locally processed</strong>, reducing transportation and import costs, making it <strong>a competitive and affordable choice</strong>.</li></ul></li></ol><h2>FAQs</h2><h4><strong>1. What is the difference between this Flaxseed Gum Powder and pure flaxseed gum?</strong></h4><p>This Flaxseed Gum Powder contains <strong>55% gum content</strong>, while <strong>pure flaxseed gum</strong> has over <strong>90% gum content</strong> and appears milky white. Since this product has a lower gum concentration, <strong>you need to use twice the amount</strong> compared to pure flaxseed gum to achieve the same thickening effect.</p><h4><strong>2. How is this product processed?</strong></h4><p>It is produced using a <strong>pure physical milling process</strong>, without chemical solvent extraction. This ensures <strong>no chemical residues</strong> and maintains <strong>100% natural flaxseed composition</strong>, making it safer and more natural for food applications.</p><h4><strong>3. Is this product classified as a food ingredient or a food additive?</strong></h4><p>This product is classified as a <strong>food ingredient</strong> rather than a food additive. It can also be referred to as <strong>flaxseed powder</strong> and should be declared as <strong>flaxseed powder</strong> in customs clearance.</p><h4><strong>4. Where is the raw material sourced from?</strong></h4><p>The flaxseed used in this product comes from <strong>Inner Mongolia, China</strong>, a region known for its <strong>cold climate and nutrient-rich soil</strong>, which enhances the quality and gum content of the flaxseed shells used in production.</p><h4><strong>5. What are the main applications of this Flaxseed Gum Powder?</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Food industry</strong>: Used in bread, cakes, oat-b